{"id": "EUVD-2026-86640", "enisaUuid": "422be2b0-9706-3481-a119-b942742c451b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvirtio_input: stop callbacks before unregistering input device\n\nvirtinput_remove() unregisters the input device before resetting the\nvirtio device. virtinput_recv_events() drops vi->lock around input_event(),\nso clearing vi->ready does not stop a callback that passed the entry check.\nIt can still use vi->idev, requeue buffers and kick the queue.\n\nReset first, as virtinput_freeze() already does. With the preceding core\nchange, reset waits for callbacks before input_unregister_device() can\nfree vi->idev. Recheck vi->ready after taking the lock again: keep draining\ncompleted events so an input packet is not truncated, but stop requeueing\nbuffers and kicking the queue.\n\nWith evdev attached, input_unregister_handle() currently waits for an RCU\ngrace period, which also waits out IRQ callbacks. This masks the lifetime\nbug on PCI and MMIO, but does not protect sleepable callbacks on other\ntransports.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ae729b1f8ab81d1244061872db2fb0ebb110d2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/81073bca2062c916c818f2744fbab545a5c4982b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8226aeee9b9a94cd699fbb51cb230feff46cfaf2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3ba86a270dd87460759214046dc7cbd409ac711", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5378f7945856a5ed88e6f9850bc7a68f54090135", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7808b37da0a619cf1fa541c2384e783fecc2480"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5v98-rq5r-8rxh", "CVE-2026-97986"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "40e12c66-ed41-3d08-a058-c5af8c1017e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "440783e4-4792-34bf-ae10-444b6af230c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "4b862b06-ae98-36ec-a916-9d77d43712f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45b93eaa712b19da365bc <a3ba86a270dd87460759214046dc7cbd409ac711"}, {"id": "4be5d045-1094-383d-9a8e-588992f0d325", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5462f906-dc34-3cb9-88f7-ae232b5d4338", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45b93eaa712b19da365bc <d7808b37da0a619cf1fa541c2384e783fecc2480"}, {"id": "5cca84eb-0171-348c-9b7e-2b36e0ee6d79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "783a6f18-5880-3b87-b9d6-48fe1dcfc50f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.1"}, {"id": "848d9f4b-f91a-32d6-b22a-c72973404398", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "869f156a-b2e6-3f69-8846-06cf495bdf71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "a995b945-6f6f-328c-86a6-79038e016f9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45b93eaa712b19da365bc <81073bca2062c916c818f2744fbab545a5c4982b"}, {"id": "a9ab60ea-7477-3c2d-b305-17e970ffaac3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "db906db0-af2a-37f3-8d4f-f662d2c82ed3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45b93eaa712b19da365bc <8226aeee9b9a94cd699fbb51cb230feff46cfaf2"}, {"id": "e04af4e8-2ed7-3550-819e-3b672ae796da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "271c865161c57cfabca45b93eaa712b19da365bc <5378f7945856a5ed88e6f9850bc7a68f54090135"}, {"id": "e2db910e-6152-3104-b0d1-f99b06638570